{"number": 112273, "data": "5,15,365,945", "name": "A puzzle sequence, answer unknown.", "comment": ["Possible solution is a(1) = 5; a(n) = 5 + 5 * n * A215148(n-1), giving 5, 15, 365, 945, 1755, 2795, 4065, 5565, 7295, 9255, 11445, 13865, 16515, 19395, ... . - _Michal Paulovic_, Sep 15 2023"], "link": ["Floor en Lyanne van Lamoen, <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/*/http://list.seqfan.eu/pipermail/seqfan/2005-November/043712.html\">puzzle sequences</a> from \"Ask Dr. Math\". Nov 28, 2005."], "xref": ["Cf. A215148."], "keyword": "nonn,unkn", "offset": "1,1", "author": "_N. J. A. Sloane_, Nov 24 2005", "references": 0, "revision": 34, "time": "2024-12-23T14:53:42-05:00", "created": "2006-01-24T03:00:00-05:00"}